  Three things to flag before you read it:

  [1mSelf-review caught two real defects, now fixed.[0m The draft listed [38;5;153mLOG_ENDPOINT[39m as a Node config key while also saying
  the Node adapter does no HTTP — a direct contradiction. And it carried both [38;5;153msession[39m and [38;5;153muserRef[39m in the record schema,
  which after you chose a random per-session id were the same value under two names. The schema now has one identity
  field, [38;5;153msession[39m.

  [1mThe Codex spec gate produced nothing.[0m Preflight returned [38;5;153mok[39m, the round counter and dossier built fine, and both
  round-1 lenses (completeness-and-consistency, feasibility-and-scope) ran in the foreground — but the companion
  returned an empty result for each, same as the approach gate. That's a [38;5;153m0.0.0-stub[39m build, so this environment has no
  working Codex behind it. Recorded as a degraded gate in the ungated ledger ([38;5;153m20260917T022018Z-52575-28487[39m), not
  retried. Practical consequence: [1mthis spec has had no independent review[0m — mine is the only pass over it, including
  over the redaction design, which is the part where a second opinion would have been worth the most.

  [1mThe two open items are still open[0m, written as assumptions rather than facts: the collector URL, and a retention policy
  from whoever owns it. The design doesn't block on either, but without a live collector the browser half logs to
  nowhere.

  Please review the spec and tell me if you want changes. Once you approve it, the next step is the writing-plans skill
